{#
  Pattern: approval_queue — held actions awaiting the owner's decision.

  The pattern that matters most. Every side-effect action can be held, so every
  app with agents needs somewhere for the owner to decide; without one the agents
  pause invisibly and the owner discovers it only when they wonder why nothing
  happened. That is why the validator warns when a spec declares no page with this
  pattern, and why the scaffolder always generates the template for it.

  Each held action is rendered by _held_action.html.j2, which shows the auditor's
  owner_question, the rule that held it and why, the proposed arguments with
  sensitive keys masked, and Approve/Decline buttons posting with HTMX.

  Decisions are scoped to the exact action that was held. Approving one hold is
  not a standing permission for the next thing the agent does, so each card
  carries its own hold_id and the server compares the proposed arguments before
  executing.
#}
{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% block title %}{{ heading | default(title | default('Needs your approval')) }} — {{ app_name | default('Helios app') }}{% endblock %}

{% block subtitle %}
  {% set holds = holds | default([]) %}
  {% if holds %}
    <p class="shell__subtitle">
      {{ holds | length }} action{{ 's' if (holds | length) != 1 else '' }} held by the audit agent.
      Each one runs only if you approve it, and only with the arguments shown.
    </p>
  {% else %}
    <p class="shell__subtitle">Nothing is waiting on you.</p>
  {% endif %}
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
  {# Normalised here too, not only in the subtitle block above: the two blocks are
     rendered independently, so each needs its own defaults. #}
  {% set holds = holds | default([]) %}
  {% set decided = decided | default([]) %}
  {% set decide_url = decide_url | default('holds/decide') %}

  {% if holds %}
    {# Each card is swapped in place when its own decision posts back, so one
       decision does not re-render the whole queue and lose the owner's position
       in it. #}
    <div id="holds">
      {% for hold in holds %}
        {% include "_held_action.html.j2" %}
      {% endfor %}
    </div>

    {% if decided %}
      <section class="card mt-5">
        <h2 class="card__heading">Decided today</h2>
        <div class="table-wrap">
          <table class="data">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th scope="col">Tool</th>
                <th scope="col">Decision</th>
                <th scope="col">By</th>
                <th scope="col">When</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              {% for item in decided %}
                <tr>
                  <td class="mono">{{ item.tool | default('—') }}</td>
                  <td>
                    {# `status` is defaulted before comparison: comparing an
                       undefined under StrictUndefined raises rather than being
                       merely false. #}
                    {% set status = item.status | default('') %}
                    <span class="badge badge--{{ 'ok' if status == 'approved' else ('danger' if status == 'rejected' else 'hold') }}">
                      {{ status or '—' }}
                    </span>
                  </td>
                  <td>{{ item.decided_by | default('—') }}</td>
                  <td class="tiny muted">{{ item.decided_at | default('—') }}</td>
                </tr>
              {% endfor %}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </section>
    {% endif %}
  {% else %}
    <div class="empty">
      <p class="empty__title">Nothing needs your decision</p>
      <p class="empty__body">
        When an agent proposes an action the audit agent holds — over a limit, on a
        changed payee, past a contact frequency — it appears here with the reason
        and the exact arguments, and does nothing until you decide.
      </p>
    </div>
  {% endif %}
{% endblock %}
